{"key":"enterprise/T1195.002","id":"T1195.002","name":"Compromise Software Supply Chain","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1195","tactics":["initial-access"],"platforms":["Linux","Windows","macOS"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may manipulate application software prior to receipt by a final consumer for the purpose of data or system compromise. Supply chain compromise of software can take place in a number of ways, including manipulation of the application source code, manipulation of the update/distribution mechanism for that software, or replacing compiled releases with a modified version. Targeting may be specific to a desired victim set or may be…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1195/002","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--bd369cd9-abb8-41ce-b5bb-fff23ee86c00","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:49:18.341Z","source_object_version":"1.1","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0079","name":"Driver Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0079","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3551476e-14f5-4e48-a518-e82135329e03","page":"telemetry/DC0079/"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0059","name":"File Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0059","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--639e87f3-acb6-448a-9645-258f20da4bc5","page":"telemetry/DC0059/"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0078","name":"Network Traffic Flow","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0078","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--a7f22107-02e5-4982-9067-6625d4a1765a","page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"id":"DC0063","name":"Windows Registry Key Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0063","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--da85d358-741a-410d-9433-20d6269a6170","page":"telemetry/DC0063/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0309","name":"Compromised software/update chain (installer/write → first-run/child → egress/signature anomaly)","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0309","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--77d3b532-9c4f-4f9f-9581-3009b201435d","relationship_id":"relationship--91cd8b1f-5c87-41be-b7e7-310d4c6b6c3e"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0862","name":"Analytic 0862","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0309#AN0862","guidance":"Adversary ships a tampered application or update: an updater/installer (msiexec/setup/update.exe/vendor service) writes or replaces binaries; on first run it spawns scripts/shells or unsigned DLLs and beacons to non-approved update CDNs/hosts. Detection correlates: (1) process creation of installer/updater → (2) file metadata changes in program paths → (3) first-run children and module/signature anomalies → (4) outbound connections to unexpected hosts within a short window.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0309"},{"id":"AN0863","name":"Analytic 0863","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0309#AN0863","guidance":"A compromised package/update (deb/rpm/tarball/AppImage/vendor updater) is installed, writing/overwriting files in /usr/local/bin, /usr/bin, /opt, or ~/.local; first run executes unexpected shells/curl/wget and connects to unapproved hosts. Correlate package/updater execution → file writes/replace → first-run child processes → egress.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0309"},{"id":"AN0864","name":"Analytic 0864","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0309#AN0864","guidance":"A tampered app/pkg/notarized update is installed via installer, softwareupdated, Homebrew, or vendor updater; new Mach-O or bundle contents appear in /Applications, /Library, /usr/local or /opt/homebrew; first run spawns sh/zsh/osascript/curl and makes egress to unfamiliar domains; AMFI/Gatekeeper may log signature/notarization problems.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0309"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0862","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0309#AN0862","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0079","component":"Driver Load","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=6","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0862","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0309#AN0862","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0079/"},{"component_id":"DC0016","component":"Module Load","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=7","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0862","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0309#AN0862","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"component_id":"DC0039","component":"File Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=11","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0862","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0309#AN0862","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"component_id":"DC0063","component":"Windo